[1.571, "o", "COMPETITOR TABLE -- specs/igla/coder/benchmark.t27\r\n\r\n  records                     168\r\n  distinct function names     168   (0 redefinition(s))\r\n  papers entered twice        14\r\n  records citing no score     141   of 168\r\n  stating zero at pass@1      144   (3 of them cite a nonzero score elsewhere)\r\n\r\n  one paper, two competitors:\r\n    arXiv:2603.08738  formal_rtl_competitor + formalrtl_competitor\r\n                  prints as FormalRTL\r\n    arXiv:2603.27630  rtlseek_competitor + rtlseek_competitor_2\r\n                  prints as RTLSeek\r\n    arXiv:2604.25183  kuleuven_ternary_competitor + ternary_lut_generator_competitor\r\n                  prints as KU-Leuven-Ternary / Ternary LUT Generator\r\n    arXiv:2605.07782  ckt_formalizer_competitor + cktformalizer_competitor\r\n                  prints as CktFormalizer\r\n    arXiv:2606.02358  chimera_competitor + chimera_competitor_2\r\n                  prints as CHIMERA\r\n    arXiv:2606.04246  stepprm_rtl_competitor + stepprm_rtl_competitor_2 + stepprm_rtl_competitor_3 +"]
[1.571, "o", " stepprm_rtl_competitor_4\r\n                  prints as StepPRM-RTL\r\n    arXiv:2606.05253  alpha_rtl_competitor + alpha_rtl_competitor_2 + alpha_rtl_competitor_update\r\n                  prints as Alpha-RTL\r\n    arXiv:2606.05680  cass_rtl_competitor + cass_rtl_competitor_2 + cass_rtl_competitor_3\r\n                  prints as CASS-RTL\r\n    arXiv:2606.06530  rtlscout_competitor + rtlscout_competitor_2 + rtlscout_competitor_3\r\n                  prints as RTLScout\r\n    arXiv:2606.08976  rtlbenchls_competitor + rtlbenchls_competitor_2\r\n                  prints as RTL-BenchLS\r\n    arXiv:2606.09867  estrtl_competitor + estrtl_competitor_2 + estrtl_competitor_3\r\n                  prints as EstRTL\r\n    arXiv:2606.10285  openrtlset_competitor + openrtlset_competitor_2\r\n                  prints as OpenRTLSet\r\n    arXiv:2606.13706  hiersva_competitor + hiersva_competitor_update\r\n                  prints as HierSVA\r\n    arXiv:2606.15500  llm4rtl_2026_competitor + llm4rtl_2026_competitor_2 + llm4rtl_competitor + llm4rtl_comp"]
[1.5711, "o", "etitor_2\r\n"]
[1.5711, "o", "                  prints as LLM4RTL / LLM4RTL-2026\r\n\r\n  A paper is attributed to a record only from the contiguous run of `///`\r\n  lines directly above its `pub fn`. A wider window reads the previous\r\n  record's citation as this one's: that window reported 16 papers here,\r\n  and ten of them were the neighbour's.\r\n\r\n  `pass_at_1: 0.0` is the value a record takes when there is no published\r\n  score to cite -- the struct has no other way to say it. It is in range and\r\n  it is what `compare_with_competitor` subtracts, so every one of those 144\r\n  records yields our own score as the margin over it at pass@1. Read the\r\n  two counts apart: 141 records cite nothing at any metric, and 3 state zero\r\n  at pass@1 while citing a nonzero score at some OTHER k -- true citations\r\n  that still read as zero to the default comparison.\r\n"]
